{"uid":"24fdd14ae6bba6e","name":"test_ladder_exhaustion_on_a_prose_reply_keeps_todays_safe_default","fullName":"tests.test_contract_ladder#test_ladder_exhaustion_on_a_prose_reply_keeps_todays_safe_default","historyId":"223e0474b5bd488fb9a21039d0b849c8","time":{"start":1791919461614,"stop":1791919461637,"duration":23},"description":"The hat never produces a valid `verdict_gate` payload across every\n    attempt the ladder grants -- exactly the pre-task-003 outcome for an\n    unparseable reply: the approach is archived, a composite PRD is\n    written (no approach left to try again), and the ladder made its full\n    `1 + contract_retry_max` attempts (1 reused + `contract_retry_max`\n    uncharged re-asks) before giving up.\n\n    GH #209 defect 2 changed review's answer to this same question and\n    deliberately did NOT change the verdict gate's (see\n    `test_ladder_exhaustion_holds_for_an_operator_and_never_archives`\n    above, in this same module): `_verdict_gate_verdict` still returns its\n    own `(False, None)` safe default and `_step_verdict_gate` still\n    archives the approach and writes a composite PRD over it. This is a\n    recorded decision, not an oversight -- and it is the higher-value\n    follow-up of the two siblings, because the gate archives an approach on\n    exhaustion exactly as review's did AND it is the terminal-success gate\n    every self-dev run enables. It is a near-mechanical mirror of review's\n    fix (one `T(\"paused\", \"verdict_gate_contract_unrepaired\")` edge in\n    `PEER_VERDICT_GATE_DELTA[\"verdict_gate\"]`, a third piece of state out of\n    `_verdict_gate_verdict`, one branch in `_step_verdict_gate`) and is out\n    of #209's scope. Nothing in this node's assertions changes.","descriptionHtml":"<p>The hat never produces a valid <code>verdict_gate</code> payload across every<br />\nattempt the ladder grants -- exactly the pre-task-003 outcome for an<br />\nunparseable reply: the approach is archived, a composite PRD is<br />\nwritten (no approach left to try again), and the ladder made its full<br />\n<code>1 + contract_retry_max</code> attempts (1 reused + <code>contract_retry_max</code><br />\nuncharged re-asks) before giving up.</p>\n<pre><code>GH #209 defect 2 changed review's answer to this same question and\ndeliberately did NOT change the verdict gate's (see\n`test_ladder_exhaustion_holds_for_an_operator_and_never_archives`\nabove, in this same module): `_verdict_gate_verdict` still returns its\nown `(False, None)` safe default and `_step_verdict_gate` still\narchives the approach and writes a composite PRD over it. This is a\nrecorded decision, not an oversight -- and it is the higher-value\nfollow-up of the two siblings, because the gate archives an approach on\nexhaustion exactly as review's did AND it is the terminal-success gate\nevery self-dev run enables. It is a near-mechanical mirror of review's\nfix (one `T(&quot;paused&quot;, &quot;verdict_gate_contract_unrepaired&quot;)` edge in\n`PEER_VERDICT_GATE_DELTA[&quot;verdict_gate&quot;]`, a third piece of state out of\n`_verdict_gate_verdict`, one branch in `_step_verdict_gate`) and is out\nof #209's scope. Nothing in this node's assertions changes.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791919461587,"stop":1791919461587,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791919461588,"stop":1791919461595,"duration":7},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791919461595,"stop":17919